Description: Voice-to-text dictation that types into any application
 Hold a key, talk, and the words are typed into whatever application you
 are using. Speech recognition runs on this machine, so it works offline
 and nothing is sent anywhere unless AI cleanup is deliberately turned on
 and pointed at a provider.
 .
 Typing into other applications on Wayland goes through libei and the
 RemoteDesktop portal, which asks permission once and remembers it.
 python3-gi is a hard dependency for that reason: without it the grant
 cannot be stored and the permission dialog returns on every launch.
 .
 The default speech model, Parakeet TDT v3, runs on onnxruntime and is
 downloaded on first use. The Whisper engines need a runtime Debian does
 not package: either an existing whisper.cpp binary on the path, or
 faster-whisper, which the app offers to fetch into its own directory the
 first time such an engine is chosen.
